description: Layering and no-panic rules for the vTrace Rust workspace.
globs: ["crates/**", "xtask/**", "Cargo.toml", ".cargo/**"]
alwaysApply: true
---

# Rust workspace rules

- Respect the layer table in `docs/specs/0001-system-overview.md`:
  `vtrace-core` (L0) depends on no workspace crate; `vtrace-analysis`
  (L1) may depend on `vtrace-core`; `vtrace-python` (L2) may depend on
  `vtrace-core` and `vtrace-analysis`. Nothing below L2 depends on
  PyO3 or Python. `cargo xtask layers` enforces this.
- No `unwrap()`, `expect()`, `panic!`, `unreachable!`, `todo!`,
  `unimplemented!` in non-test code. Each production crate root carries
  `#![deny(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used, clippy::panic,
  clippy::unimplemented, clippy::todo, clippy::unreachable)]`.
- `unsafe` is `forbid` workspace-wide. If an FFI module ever needs it,
  confine it to one module with a `// SAFETY:` comment on every block
  and a safe `Result` API (mirrors the SoundCraft clap-host exception).
- Timestamps cross the FFI as `i64` ns + `clock_domain` string, never
  a raw `std::time::Instant` (spec 0001, spec 0004).
- `record()` must not block or panic; it timestamps before the queue
  and uses `try_push` into a bounded buffer (spec 0005).
- Run `cargo xtask ci` before declaring done. No performance claim
  without a benchmark run in P5.
